  "description": "A conflict story names an application policy the reference does not implement. The application records that policy's end act at the review, on the story Item, sourced from its workflow process. The story then reads ended under its policy, with the policy's cause as the ending kind and no baseline ending, while it still reads disagreeing and the sources still conflict: a policy changes no derived fact. The end act is read without policy code, and the transition check lists it as unverified, within its scope only. A policy end act carrying @effective, a second end act under the same policy, and an end act naming a policy that does not govern the story are rejected.",
